the plugin context; variables don't persist between calls. So each call must be self-contained (re-find pages, re-declare helpers). I'll define a compact helper preamble in each call.\n\nFonts: load Roboto Regular/Medium/Bold at start of each call that creates text.\n\nLet me now check what the icons/components look like via screenshots, and get details of the Button and Text Field components (fills, fonts) so my design is consistent. Also need to check icon internal structure for recoloring (instance children). Actually recoloring icons: instances can be overridden (fills on children). I can set fills on the instance's vector children.\n\nAlso need to inspect whether Logo components are images or vectors. Logo_ABNB etc. are image-filled; watchlist marks are vectors.\n\nLet me take screenshots of the components page and media page to see visuals, and also get design context via use_figma read-only queries for the Button and Text Field (fills, text style).\n\nActually, the reminder says \"MUST call get_design_context if trying to implement the design\" — but get_design_context tool isn't in my list. The available tools: get_metadata, get_screenshot, use_figma, whoami. So I can't call get_design_context; I'll use use_figma in read-only mode to inspect.\n\nNext step: screenshots of 02 Components (1:18) and 04 Media (3:49) frames, plus inspect Button/Text Field properties via use_figma.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"941e9e8f-9f13-404f-85a0-b0b25ea4fd23","uuid":"df6798af-d967-41f5-a6c5-bde2c3e4cfc4","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:15:26.383Z","thinking_duration_ms":12581}
